        <updated>2026-01-09T14:16:36.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1376607?u=186d334fc71b9f12c05d773c85f5986d279e7964&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Addresses incorrect or absent guidance related to accessible names in the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Overflow/Carousels" rel="nofollow">Creating CSS carousels</a> guide.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Devs are starting to try to implement these and creating WCAG violations without realizing it because this, along with lots of promotion in dev sites, wrongly claims these are "accessible" (without qualifying how or in what way).</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">Recent evidence of their baseline inaccessibility: <a href="https://www.sarasoueidan.com/blog/css-carousels-accessibility/" rel="nofollow">https://www.sarasoueidan.com/blog/css-carousels-accessibility/</a></p>
